    "title": "Abdominal pain: screen as suspected ADR",
    "message": "Guidelines require screening ALL patients at each encounter for suspected adverse drug reactions using the Drug Safety Screening checklist, and all suspected ADRs (mild or severe) must be recorded and reported. Patient P004 presents with new abdominal pain on TDF/3TC/DTG since March 2023. TDF can cause gastrointestinal toxicity and renal-related abdominal complaints. DTG has also been associated with gastrointestinal side effects. Evidence against drug attribution: appetite is preserved and no fever is present, suggesting a non-severe process. Non-drug causes such as gastritis, peptic ulcer disease, or functional abdominal pain should also be considered. The clinician's plan does not document ADR screening or an aDSM form.",
